Blot native Carp semantic port

The generated files contain mechanical translations of Blot compiler sources
from mewhhaha/blot2, commit 0c04639358ac64cc9c76924493748b7bca785cf3.
Blot source is copyright 2026 Jacob Torrång, under the repository's MIT license.

Standard-library functions and representation conventions derive from Bend
2.0.32, copyright 2026 HigherOrderCO, licensed under Apache License 2.0.
The translation changes the implementation language, calling convention and
memory management. Tail calls and terminal bind chains use stack-safe native
calling conventions. The request decoder validates Unicode before character
construction to preserve native error recovery. Selected list operations have been rewritten as loops;
weighted batch boundaries use the new native cooperative worker pool.
The Apache license is included in licenses/BEND-APACHE-2.0.txt.

The regeneration-only parser in vendor/acorn.cjs is Acorn 8.15.0 (MIT).
Its original notices are retained in licenses/ACORN-MIT.txt.
Neither Acorn, Node nor Bend is required to build the checked-in Carp sources
or to execute the native compiler.
